# Helper Functions Reference

<!-- @project-config:helpers-table -->
## `functions/core/helpers.php`

### `skel_init_filesystem()`

Initialize the WordPress Filesystem API and return the global `$wp_filesystem`.

### `skel_get_post_thumbnail_id( $post_id )`

Return the post's featured-image ID, or `DEFAULT_THUMBNAIL_ID` (or `0`) when none is set.

### `skel_posts_pagination( int $total_pages ): void`

Render `<nav class="posts-pagination">` with prev/next arrows for a paginated query.

### `skel_is_rtl(): bool`

True when the current WPML language is RTL (Arabic). Requires WPML.

### `skel_swiper_direction_class(): string`

Return `'swiper'` (LTR) or `'swiper-rtl'` (RTL) for the Swiper container element.

### `skel_direction_class(): string`

Return `'dir-ltr'` or `'dir-rtl'` for any element that needs language-direction styling.

### `skel_get_validate_youtube_link( string $link ): string|false`

Extract a YouTube video ID from any URL form (watch, short, embed, with params) and return a normalized `https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=…` URL, or `false` if no valid ID was found.

### `skel_get_yt_link( string $url ): string`

Wrapper around `skel_get_validate_youtube_link()` — returns the validated URL or the original input on failure.

### `skel_get_random_string( int $length = 10 ): string`

Generate a random lowercase string of the given length (uses `wp_generate_password`).

### `skel_get_the_excerpt( int $limit = 50, ?int $post_id = null ): string`

Return a word-limited excerpt with `...` appended when truncated; strips shortcodes.

### `skel_get_text_shorter( string $input, int $length ): string`

Truncate text to `$length` characters while preserving whole words; appends `...` when shortened. Multibyte-safe.

### `skel_get_the_terms_data( int $post_id, string $taxonomy ): array`

Return an array of `[ 'name' => string, 'id' => int ]` for terms attached to a post.

### `skel_get_the_terms( int $post_id, string $taxonomy, string $separator = ' ' ): string`

Return term names joined by `$separator` (no markup).

### `skel_get_phone_url( string|false $phone_number = false ): string`

Build a `tel:` URL from a phone number, stripping non-numeric characters except `+`.

### `skel_insert_page( int $id, bool $display = false ): ?string`

Apply `the_content` filters to another page's content; echo when `$display` is true.

### `skel_extract_oembed_src( ?string $html ): ?string`

Extract the `src` attribute from an oEmbed iframe HTML; converts `youtube.com` → `youtube-nocookie.com` and removes `feature=oembed`.

### `skel_get_full_url(): string`

Return the full URL of the current request (sanitized, with correct protocol).

### `skel_replace_text_with_icon( string $text ): void`

Echo `$text` after replacing `[play]` and `[play-image]` placeholders with `<i>` icon HTML.

### `skel_sanitize_superglobal( string $key, string $type = 'POST', string $default = '' ): string`

Safely read and sanitize a `$_GET` or `$_POST` value. Caller is responsible for nonces.

### `skel_is_dark_color( string $hex ): bool`

True when a hex color's WCAG-2.0 relative luminance is at or below `0.179` (i.e. needs light text).

### `skel_get_italic_braces( $text )`

Replace `{text}` → `<i>text</i>` and `[text]` → `<strong>text</strong>` in `$text`, then return kses-sanitized HTML.

### `is_login_or_registration_page(): bool`

True on `wp-login.php` / `wp-register.php`. Note: this helper is unprefixed (legacy).

## `functions/core/svg-helpers.php`

### `skel_get_svg( string $image, array $attributes = array() ): string`

Inline an SVG file from `assets/images/icons/{$image}.svg`, applying optional attributes; returns empty string on failure.

### `skel_get_svg_content( string $image, array $attributes = array() ): string|false`

Lower-level fetch used by `skel_get_svg`: reads, sanitizes, caches, and returns SVG content with attributes applied.

### `skel_sanitize_svg( string $svg_content ): string|false`

Strip dangerous elements / attributes (script, event handlers, javascript: URLs, etc.) from raw SVG content.

### `skel_get_attachment_image( int $attachment_id, string $size = 'w1400', array $attributes = array() ): string`

Render an attachment as inline SVG when its mime is `image/svg+xml`, otherwise as `wp_get_attachment_image()`.

### `skel_add_svg_attributes( string $svg_content, array $attributes = array() ): string|false`

Merge attributes onto an SVG element. Strips `width`/`height` so the SVG scales via CSS; merges with existing `class`.

## `functions/blocks-system/acf-block-helpers.php`

### `skel_get_acf_block_paths(): array`

Return the registered ACF block paths (e.g. `[ 'blocks' => '/path/to/blocks/' ]`).

### `skel_get_block_slug( string $block_name ): string`

Convert a human block name to a slug via `sanitize_title()`.

### `skel_render_block_preview( array $block ): bool`

Render the editor preview image when `$block['data']['preview_image']` is set; returns `true` if rendered so the caller can `return` early.

### `skel_should_display_block(): bool`

Return `true` unless the block's `display` field is explicitly `'off'`. Defaults to true on new blocks.

### `skel_get_block_developer_options(): array`

Return the auto-injected developer options for the current block: `display_class`, `spacing_top`, `spacing_bottom`, `spacing_top_custom`, `spacing_bottom_custom`, `custom_classes`, `custom_css`, `unique_id`.

### `skel_get_background_image_css( int $image_id, string $size = 'medium_crop' ): string`

Return a `background-image: url(...)` CSS string for the given attachment, falling back to a placeholder.

### `skel_render_block_section_open( array $dev_options, string $section_class = '' ): void`

Print the opening `<section>` for an ACF block, applying `$dev_options` (classes, custom CSS, unique ID).

### `skel_render_block_section_close(): void`

Print `</section>`. Pair with `skel_render_block_section_open()`.

### `skel_render_acf_link( $link, string $classes = 'btn', string $default_text = '' ): void`

Render an ACF link field as a properly-escaped `<a href target class>` tag.
